---
import '@fontsource-variable/familjen-grotesk';
import '../styles/global.css';
import TryIt from '../components/TryIt.svelte';
import markDark from '../../../../assets/brand/mark-dark.svg';
import markMint from '../../../../assets/brand/mark-mint.svg';

const title = 'Glassboard';
const tagline = 'Draw on your screen. Then get back to work.';
const description = 'Glassboard is a small annotation tool for macOS and Windows. One shortcut turns your whole screen into a drawing surface. Press it again and the drawings are gone.';
const repo = 'https://github.com/ImNallen/Glassboard';
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#a3e9d1" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={`${title}: ${tagline}`} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content={Astro.site} />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="any" />
    <link rel="canonical" href={Astro.site} />
    <title>{title}: {tagline}</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="top">
          <a class="brand" href="/"><img src={markDark.src} width="30" height="30" alt="" />Glassboard</a>
          <nav aria-label="Site">
            <a href={repo}>GitHub</a>
            <a href="#get">Download</a>
          </nav>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="wrap" style="margin-top: clamp(40px, 6vw, 80px)">
        <h1>{tagline}</h1>
        <p class="lede">{description}</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <button class="button primary" type="button" data-glassboard-try>Try it on this page</button>
          <span class="or">or press <kbd>⌘</kbd> <kbd>⇧</kbd> <kbd>A</kbd> <span class="win">(Ctrl Shift A on Windows)</span></span>
          <svg class="arrow" viewBox="0 0 300 150" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
            <defs>
              <linearGradient id="stroke" x1="290" y1="140" x2="40" y2="8" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
                <stop offset="0" stop-color="#f46b78" /><stop offset=".2" stop-color="#f2c85b" /><stop offset=".4" stop-color="#4dcaa0" /><stop offset=".6" stop-color="#4fc5d5" /><stop offset=".8" stop-color="#669df0" /><stop offset="1" stop-color="#a184e8" />
              </linearGradient>
            </defs>
            <path d="M290 140 C 250 60, 170 20, 40 8" stroke="url(#stroke)" stroke-width="5" stroke-linecap="round" />
            <path d="M76 2 L40 8 L64 38" stroke="url(#stroke)" stroke-width="5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
          </svg>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section id="how">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="section-head">
            <h2>Three keystrokes, start to finish</h2>
            <p>Glassboard lives in the menu bar or system tray and stays out of the way until you need it.</p>
          </div>
          <ol class="steps">
            <li>
              <h3>Press the shortcut</h3>
              <p>A mint glow along the edges of every display shows you're annotating. Your windows stay exactly where they were.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Draw over anything</h3>
              <p>Arrows, pen strokes, squares, circles, a highlighter, and text, on every screen at once. Hold Shift for straight arrows and equal-sided shapes.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Press it again</h3>
              <p>Glassboard hides and clears every display. The next session starts clean, so there's nothing to tidy up.</p>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="tools">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="section-head">
            <h2>Every tool has a key</h2>
            <p>The toolbar tucks into a thin pill at the edge of the screen. Move the cursor near it to open it, or skip it entirely and use the shortcuts.</p>
          </div>
          <table class="tools">
            <thead>
              <tr><th scope="col">Tool</th><th scope="col">What it does</th><th scope="col">Mac (Windows uses Ctrl)</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Arrow</td><td><p>Point at the thing you mean.</p></td><td><kbd>⌘</kbd><kbd>1</kbd></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Pen</td><td><p>Freehand strokes that follow your hand.</p></td><td><kbd>⌘</kbd><kbd>2</kbd></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Square</td><td><p>Frame a region. Shift keeps it square.</p></td><td><kbd>⌘</kbd><kbd>3</kbd></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Circle</td><td><p>Ring something. Shift keeps it round.</p></td><td><kbd>⌘</kbd><kbd>4</kbd></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Highlighter</td><td><p>A translucent stroke for text and rows.</p></td><td><kbd>⌘</kbd><kbd>H</kbd></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Text</td><td><p>Click, type, press Enter.</p></td><td><kbd>⌘</kbd><kbd>T</kbd></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Eraser</td><td><p>Drag across marks to remove them as one undo step.</p></td><td><kbd>⌘</kbd><kbd>E</kbd></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Undo, redo</td><td><p>Within the current session.</p></td><td><kbd>⌘</kbd><kbd>Z</kbd> <kbd>⌘</kbd><kbd>⇧</kbd><kbd>Z</kbd></td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <ul class="palette" aria-label="Colors">
            <li><span class="dot rainbow"></span>Rainbow shifts hue as you drag</li>
            <li><span class="dot" style="background: conic-gradient(#f46b78 0 120deg, #4dcaa0 120deg 240deg, #669df0 240deg 360deg)"></span>Shifting picks a new color per shape</li>
            <li><span class="dot" style="background: #000"></span>Black</li>
            <li><span class="dot" style="background: #fff"></span>White</li>
            <li><span class="dot" style="background: #4dcaa0"></span>Green</li>
            <li><span class="dot" style="background: #f2c85b"></span>Yellow</li>
            <li><span class="dot" style="background: #f46b78"></span>Red</li>
            <li><span class="dot" style="background: #669df0"></span>Blue</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="extras">Colors are the number keys 1 to 8. Marks can fade on their own after 3, 5, or 10 seconds, or stay until you return to work. The toolbar docks to the left, right, or bottom edge.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="local">
        <div class="wrap two-col">
          <h2>Runs on your machine, and only there</h2>
          <div class="prose">
            <p><strong>There is no account, no server, and no screen recording.</strong> The built app never touches the network. Your preferences are a small JSON file in the app's configuration folder, and drawings live in memory until you hide the overlay.</p>
            <p>Glassboard is written in Rust and Svelte on Tauri 2, so the whole thing is a few megabytes and starts instantly. The source is public, and every feature on this page was built in the open.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="get" class="get">
        <div class="wrap">
          <h2>Get Glassboard</h2>
          <p>Glassboard runs on macOS and Windows. Signed installers aren't published yet, so for now, build it from source. With Node.js and Rust installed it's two commands: <code>npm ci</code> and <code>npm run desktop tauri build</code>.</p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="button primary" href={`${repo}#run-locally`}>Build it from source</a>
            <a class="button quiet" href={repo}>Star the repository</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <div class="wrap">
        <span>Glassboard is open source. <a href={repo}>Source on GitHub</a>.</span>
        <span>Everything on this page runs locally in your browser.</span>
      </div>
    </footer>

    <TryIt client:only="svelte" />
  </body>
</html>
